**The tools were designed as separate layers with no native bridge – the user is manually transporting data between two systems that were never built to talk to each other**

This is an architectural problem because the social layer (X, Telegram, Discord) where signals 
and contract addresses appear is completely disconnected from the execution layer (DEX interfaces, wallets).
Users are forced to act as the human bridge between two systems that were never designed to integrate — copying, pasting,
and switching contexts manually. No amount of speed improvement fixes this fundamental separation;
it requires an architectural change where execution can happen natively *within* the feed where signals appear.
